<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20253" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harpē</span></b> , ēs,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅρπη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A sickleshaped sword</i>, <i>a
				falchion</i>, <i>cimeter</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5,
			69</span></i>; <i><span class="en">176</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 9,
			663</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 4, 388</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A species of falcon</i>, <i>tassel
				gentle</i>: Falco gentilis, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 10,
				74, 95, § 204</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
